Thanks, confirmed: the deprecations page now lists `gpt-6-luna` as the replacement for `gpt-5-nano`, so the "recommended replacement: `gpt-5.6-luna`" line in the description is out of date.

@jverre which default would you like? This PR currently uses `gpt-5.6-luna`, which should keep working past the 2026-12-11 shutdown of `gpt-5-nano`. If you'd rather follow OpenAI's listed replacement, I can switch both the Python and TypeScript SDKs to `gpt-6-luna` here, after checking how the SDKs handle its parameters and tool calls.


